WEBVTT

01:30.680 --> 01:33.560
Wowie wow! Coco, you're so fast!

01:37.740 --> 01:39.830
You <i>are</i> going fast!

01:39.830 --> 01:45.000
So it was your Sylph Shoes that had 
Agott flying so fast earlier, huh?

01:47.230 --> 01:50.100
Wh-Wh-What did I do to Agott?!

01:50.100 --> 01:51.380
She's fine.

01:51.850 --> 01:56.140
If she's still using them, 
she must have liked your spell.

01:58.010 --> 02:00.480
Straight lines are your 
specialty, after all.

01:58.770 --> 02:02.140
Agott likes... my spell?

02:00.480 --> 02:02.940
That might help you out 
with other spells, too.

02:02.940 --> 02:05.530
Stop that, Master. Coco's not listening.

02:05.840 --> 02:07.770
I'm a Smartygott, too...

02:08.570 --> 02:10.080
Master Qifrey?

02:15.020 --> 02:16.740
What is it, Master?

02:17.280 --> 02:18.630
This isn't good.

02:19.260 --> 02:20.920
It's Alaira's hat.

02:21.620 --> 02:24.250
Hats are special to witches.

02:24.250 --> 02:26.170
We don't let them go unless—

02:31.550 --> 02:33.200
<i>A golem?!</i>

02:33.200 --> 02:35.930
<i>A forbidden spell this ancient 
shouldn't still be active!</i>

02:36.310 --> 02:40.140
<i>The Brimmed Caps are behind this!</i>

02:41.610 --> 02:43.230
Master Qifrey?!

02:49.060 --> 02:54.950
<b>For bidden Magic</b>

02:55.840 --> 02:58.380
Wh-Where are we supposed to run away <i>to</i>?!

02:58.840 --> 03:03.440
That was... a Brimmed Cap!

03:04.290 --> 03:06.040
We can't possibly ge—

03:06.040 --> 03:07.570
Grr.

03:20.820 --> 03:23.810
Well, isn't that something?

03:23.810 --> 03:26.700
You actually managed to hide from me...

03:28.940 --> 03:32.040
I just <i>love</i> hide-and-seek.

03:32.800 --> 03:35.320
I know you're there.

03:46.350 --> 03:49.740
Huh? I'm the only one whose cloak...

03:58.460 --> 04:01.150
Who hides themselves in darkness?

04:01.150 --> 04:05.100
Sinners trying to hide 
their nasty little secrets...

04:05.440 --> 04:08.780
Weaklings driven by fear, 
trying to protect themselves...

04:09.230 --> 04:12.710
And hunters lying in wait of their prey.

04:13.610 --> 04:17.250
Which of those are you, I wonder?

04:19.090 --> 04:19.950
It disappeared!

04:19.950 --> 04:23.120
I can say you're not hunters...

04:23.740 --> 04:27.210
because <i>I'm</i> the hunter here.

04:30.210 --> 04:31.310
Euini!

04:33.880 --> 04:35.500
Help!

04:35.500 --> 04:36.710
Close your eyes!

04:36.710 --> 04:37.560
Richeh!

04:39.530 --> 04:40.740
Euini!

04:41.510 --> 04:42.990
Can you get up?

04:43.540 --> 04:44.860
Richeh, let's go!

04:44.860 --> 04:47.410
You can stay here and talk to the dust!

04:52.020 --> 04:56.030
<i>We can't fly away because 
of the spell cast on the cave.</i>

04:56.460 --> 04:59.820
<i>Even if we stretch out the stones, 
there's only so far we can go.</i>

04:59.820 --> 05:03.700
<i>This isn't someone we can think 
or trick our way around.</i>

05:04.120 --> 05:06.710
<i>Even Alaira couldn't beat them.</i>

05:06.710 --> 05:08.120
<i>As I am now...</i>

05:16.670 --> 05:18.040
That's it!

05:18.430 --> 05:19.920
Agott?!

05:19.920 --> 05:22.530
When Alaira crossed the gap in the road,

05:22.530 --> 05:24.550
she froze the air under 
her feet and slid along.

05:27.250 --> 05:31.530
If we freeze the road itself, we won't 
have to worry about gaps in the seals.

05:33.440 --> 05:34.740
This should do it.

05:45.980 --> 05:48.240
Sliding along will be 
faster than running!

05:53.460 --> 05:54.850
Ready, Richeh?

05:54.850 --> 05:55.900
Get on!

05:56.710 --> 05:58.420
Come on! Hurry!

06:12.020 --> 06:16.040
A-Agott! Why are your 
Sylph Shoes so fast?!

06:16.040 --> 06:17.720
I don't want to talk about it!

06:17.720 --> 06:20.530
Quickly, freeze the path further ahead!

06:20.530 --> 06:21.690
R-Right!

06:34.080 --> 06:36.090
He's going to catch up to us.

06:36.090 --> 06:37.790
Use a wind spell to push us faster!

06:37.790 --> 06:38.860
I...

06:40.750 --> 06:47.090
I d-don't know a lot of other spells.

06:47.090 --> 06:48.740
H-Here.

06:51.310 --> 06:54.060
Y-You can use mine.

06:54.440 --> 06:57.750
Filling it up in advance was pathetic, 
but now I'm glad I did.

06:59.550 --> 07:01.540
It'll help you.

07:21.460 --> 07:26.470
<i>Why did this have to happen to us 
after my big chance to take the test?!</i>

07:26.470 --> 07:28.610
Why did this have to—

07:30.160 --> 07:35.230
<i>Tetia said the same thing while 
we were running from the dragon.</i>

07:35.660 --> 07:39.860
<i>This kind of calamity doesn't 
befall ordinary apprentices.</i>

07:40.270 --> 07:43.750
<i>The special thing the 
Brimmed Caps are after...</i>

07:44.430 --> 07:46.290
<i>It's not us.</i>

07:51.740 --> 07:53.100
Agott?!

07:53.870 --> 07:57.290
The person you're looking for isn't here!

07:57.290 --> 08:00.690
You remember when the 
Knights Moralis took flight before?

08:00.690 --> 08:04.170
They erased her memory and 
returned her to her village!

08:04.540 --> 08:07.930
So chasing us won't get you anywhere!

08:08.940 --> 08:13.310
The Outsider isn't at our atelier anymore!

08:17.180 --> 08:21.620
Spoken just like an apprentice 
to those long-time, world-class liars,

08:21.620 --> 08:24.690
the Pointed Caps.

08:25.130 --> 08:28.570
A persuasive deception 
from the student of a liar.

08:29.440 --> 08:30.610
Agott!

08:33.330 --> 08:34.070
Agott?!

08:34.070 --> 08:35.140
Agott!

08:36.860 --> 08:38.460
Poor little dear...

08:39.730 --> 08:43.230
The Pointed Caps of 
the past were sinners.

08:43.230 --> 08:48.050
The Pointed Caps of the present are 
weaklings who fear their own power.

08:48.590 --> 08:53.720
It is because of them that you 
remain stifled by their rules,

08:53.720 --> 08:56.780
unable to expand your potential.

09:00.840 --> 09:03.730
<i>This smell... Conjuring Ink?</i>

09:04.210 --> 09:06.720
Your salvation lies in forbidden magic.

09:06.720 --> 09:08.990
Have you never dreamed of more?

09:09.510 --> 09:12.740
If you wanted, you could 
grow up this instant.

09:13.080 --> 09:16.490
You could make a world where 
you could remain a child forever.

09:17.090 --> 09:20.440
A world where you don't 
have to hide your spells.

09:20.440 --> 09:23.480
Where you could become your ideal self...

09:24.000 --> 09:27.880
One where you could 
fly without using shoes.

09:28.400 --> 09:30.790
Where you could go wherever you wanted!

09:30.790 --> 09:35.610
Why, I've even liberated myself 
from the shackles of flesh!

09:36.010 --> 09:39.080
Soon enough, the world will remember...

09:39.080 --> 09:44.850
which kind of hat witches 
were meant to wear.

09:44.850 --> 09:50.980
We simply seek to hasten 
that moment's arrival.

09:51.900 --> 09:56.070
For that, sacrifices must be made.

09:56.070 --> 09:57.410
Agott!

09:58.770 --> 10:01.610
Once she sees the harm that 
has befallen a precious friend

10:01.610 --> 10:03.630
who even lied to save her...

10:03.630 --> 10:07.200
If I were to offer her 
the tool of your salvation,

10:07.200 --> 10:13.220
would she be able to turn down 
the miracle our magic offers?

10:14.940 --> 10:17.420
Children don't wish to face the tests of life,

10:17.420 --> 10:20.310
but it is how they learn and grow.

10:20.310 --> 10:24.660
This is my test for her.

10:25.530 --> 10:29.320
I think you will make...

10:29.320 --> 10:31.110
an excellent lesson.

10:37.060 --> 10:42.000
<i>The Brimmed Caps sometimes 
tattoo seals onto themselves.</i>

10:43.640 --> 10:44.960
You're not going to...

10:44.960 --> 10:47.130
No! Don't you dare!

10:47.130 --> 10:50.590
I'm not going to lose everything to this!

10:51.380 --> 10:53.500
I still haven't shown that person—

10:55.470 --> 10:57.220
Agott!

10:57.990 --> 11:00.720
When you fall, grab this!

11:01.220 --> 11:03.480
When I fall?

11:20.410 --> 11:22.360
What caused that explosion?

11:22.360 --> 11:24.750
Euini broke the path from beneath.

11:25.530 --> 11:28.750
If you leave the road, you get 
caught up in the labyrinth cave.

11:29.240 --> 11:32.530
So we had the idea to break 
the road under his feet.

11:34.240 --> 11:36.010
But...

11:36.010 --> 11:38.140
That Brimmed Cap...

11:38.140 --> 11:40.660
has been flying around the whole time.

11:42.640 --> 11:45.150
<i>Looks like Agott's safe.</i>

11:45.150 --> 11:47.140
<i>I'm so glad it worked out!</i>

11:50.980 --> 11:56.030
<i>To think covering up for my deficiencies 
could lead to something this useful...</i>

11:56.030 --> 11:57.720
<i>I'm so happy.</i>

11:57.720 --> 12:00.410
<i>Maybe I'm not so hopeless after all!</i>

12:01.410 --> 12:03.710
Listen to me, Master!

12:03.710 --> 12:07.450
I... I'm not as hopeless 
as I thought I was.

12:07.910 --> 12:11.620
I wasn't as hopeless as you said I was!

12:14.760 --> 12:18.330
Master might not understand,

12:18.330 --> 12:20.770
but the fact that I can't do all 
the same things as everyone else

12:20.770 --> 12:23.610
might be a chance to do different things!

12:23.610 --> 12:25.440
That's right!

12:27.700 --> 12:31.990
And if you'd just used your specialty 
and remained hidden away,

12:31.990 --> 12:34.650
I might have been willing to spare you.

12:35.520 --> 12:36.730
Help—

12:35.520 --> 12:38.810
Those who cloak themselves in shadow 
should have more of a dark side.

12:38.810 --> 12:41.680
I think you're lacking there.

12:42.180 --> 12:48.300
I'll give you a form 
you'll truly wish to hide.

12:50.360 --> 12:52.790
Always flying?

12:52.790 --> 12:55.060
That's really weird.

12:55.420 --> 12:59.440
Any person or spell that 
leaves the surface of the road

12:59.440 --> 13:03.090
should be affected by the 
Romonons' ancient spell.

13:03.640 --> 13:07.550
If the Brimmed Cap isn't affected, 
it means we're still in danger!

13:08.210 --> 13:11.900
Call Euini. We have to 
get back to Master Qifrey.

13:11.900 --> 13:13.230
Euini!

13:13.230 --> 13:14.120
Euini!

13:14.120 --> 13:15.900
Euini!

13:21.810 --> 13:23.060
Euini?

14:06.820 --> 14:09.120
A-Agott...

14:09.120 --> 14:10.720
Richeh...

14:11.190 --> 14:13.820
Please, sa...

14:15.090 --> 14:20.310
Feel myself... vani... shi...

14:50.990 --> 14:53.610
E-Euini...

14:59.650 --> 15:00.600
Richeh!

15:00.600 --> 15:02.090
Agott, what do we do?!

15:02.090 --> 15:03.990
Euini... Euini's...

15:07.960 --> 15:10.360
Isn't that interesting?

15:10.360 --> 15:15.350
To think it would integrate the 
scalewolf fur used to make the cloak...

15:15.350 --> 15:16.480
You...

15:16.480 --> 15:21.750
Research on forbidden spells has 
stagnated since its loss to time.

15:21.750 --> 15:25.600
We frequently don't know what 
they'll do until we use them.

15:25.600 --> 15:28.420
The result wasn't what I expected,

15:28.420 --> 15:30.770
but it works well enough.

15:30.770 --> 15:34.750
Stop spewing garbage and turn Euini back!

15:34.750 --> 15:37.780
If you want to save him...

15:38.360 --> 15:41.490
be my guest.

15:41.490 --> 15:44.690
Magic has the power 
to grant all our wishes.

15:44.690 --> 15:48.130
What happens next is entirely up to you.

16:02.310 --> 16:04.150
Where are you going, Richeh?

16:05.600 --> 16:08.660
Where do you think? 
I'm going to save Euini.

16:09.790 --> 16:10.810
I...

16:11.280 --> 16:14.280
I don't want to do things 
I don't want to do,

16:14.280 --> 16:17.100
but even more than that, 
I don't want to abandon a friend!

16:18.180 --> 16:20.290
You don't feel the same way?

16:20.290 --> 16:23.800
I do. But we have a responsibility.

16:24.340 --> 16:26.870
The myrphons are terrified. 
What about them?

16:27.230 --> 16:28.840
I know this is no time for tests,

16:28.840 --> 16:31.380
but we have to get them 
back to their flock.

16:32.270 --> 16:35.920
And someone has to tell people 
what happened here.

16:35.920 --> 16:38.170
About Alaira and Euini...

16:39.390 --> 16:41.270
Let's split up.

16:41.760 --> 16:43.750
I'll go after Euini.

16:43.750 --> 16:46.000
You get the myrphons to the exit.

16:46.000 --> 16:47.870
No! I'm going after Euini!

16:47.870 --> 16:49.130
Why do you get to decide?!

16:49.130 --> 16:51.730
I know more spells.

16:51.730 --> 16:53.320
I'm more adaptable.

16:53.890 --> 16:57.990
The spells you learned are 
biased toward things you like.

16:57.990 --> 17:01.090
You can't be flexible in 
unexpected circumstances.

17:01.960 --> 17:04.210
I'm sorry to be harsh,

17:04.210 --> 17:07.860
but you can't be any help 
to Euini as you are now.

18:20.340 --> 18:22.000
Brushbuddy?

18:49.470 --> 18:51.610
<i>What happened back there?</i>

18:51.610 --> 18:53.500
<i>The serpent gate attacked us...</i>

18:54.030 --> 18:56.130
<i>The ground caved in...</i>

18:56.850 --> 19:01.080
<i>Then... Master protected me.</i>

19:03.840 --> 19:05.280
Master Qifrey...

19:06.020 --> 19:07.310
Tetia...

19:16.120 --> 19:19.300
<i>Master... He's hurt.</i>

19:20.090 --> 19:23.060
<i>His glasses are broken. He's bleeding.</i>

19:33.850 --> 19:37.030
I-I'm sorry.

19:37.410 --> 19:40.770
Your glasses were cracked, so I thought...

19:40.770 --> 19:42.980
Hush. Be quiet.

19:51.160 --> 19:52.530
Something's out there.

20:13.460 --> 20:15.400
Witches.

20:16.280 --> 20:18.320
Witches stand among us.

20:18.680 --> 20:21.750
Those who changed us into these forms...

20:21.750 --> 20:25.830
Vile... Vile witches...

20:26.580 --> 20:29.610
Master, are those...

20:29.610 --> 20:30.860
Yes.

20:30.860 --> 20:35.450
The old people of Romonon, 
transformed alive into gold decorations...

20:37.110 --> 20:38.220
Master!

20:37.110 --> 20:38.220
Master!

20:40.610 --> 20:42.470
You're hurt so badly...

20:44.450 --> 20:49.480
They hold a deep resentment 
toward witches.

20:52.890 --> 20:57.970
Therefore, we'll have to assume 
they'll attack us when they can.

21:01.250 --> 21:03.780
Stay right where you are.

21:04.610 --> 21:07.010
They won't notice you then.

21:07.650 --> 21:12.050
It looks like my cloak's spell is ruined.

21:13.170 --> 21:16.180
Because you protected us...

21:20.600 --> 21:22.120
I will protect you

21:23.000 --> 21:25.960
because I'm your master.

21:34.240 --> 21:36.600
Listen, you two.

21:38.660 --> 21:40.890
Stay close to me.

21:45.390 --> 21:46.890
As close as you can.
